  "id": "conjunction",
  "term": "conjunction",
  "definition": "In cognitive judgments about probability, a conjunction is the combined occurrence of two events, such as A and B happening together. In research on conjunction fallacies, people may incorrectly judge this combined event as more likely than one or both of the single events.",
